{"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent\/privacymanifests"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"What each module can collect, the required-reason APIs it calls, and the privacy manifest it ships, so you can fill in your app’s own manifest and privacy labels.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Traffluent collects nothing on its own. It records only the events your app tracks and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"context your app turns on: every kind of automatic instrumentation and every standard enricher is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"opt in. It sends records only to the destinations your app gives a delivery, to endpoints your app"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"names. None of it is used for tracking as Apple defines it: no module links what it records with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other companies’ data, reads the advertising identifier, fingerprints the device, or works around"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the user’s consent or App Tracking Transparency. Every manifest declares "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyTracking"},{"type":"text","text":" as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"type":"text","text":" and lists no tracking domains."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each module that can produce data of one of Apple’s collected data types ships a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" declaring it. SwiftPM and Bazel both put it in a resource bundle named"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Traffluent_<Module>.bundle","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which Xcode and rules_apple copy into your app, where Xcode’s privacy"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"report finds it. A module your app doesn’t link adds nothing to the report."}]},{"level":3,"anchor":"Required-reason-APIs","text":"Required-reason APIs","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"No Traffluent module calls an API on Apple’s list of required-reason APIs, so every manifest’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is empty. The list’s categories are file timestamps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), system boot time","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategorySystemBootTime","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), disk space","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryDiskSpace","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), active keyboards","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryActiveKeyboards","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") and user defaults","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). The modules that come nearest:","type":"text"}]},{"header":"row","type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Module"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"What it calls"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Why none is a required-reason API"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","isActive":true}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text